          "gap": 10,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "wMqAT",
              "name": "Tag",
              "fill": "$accent",
              "content": "DIRECTION D · SYNTHESIS",
              "fontFamily": "$mono",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "T6aLvx",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$fg",
              "content": "One app, three independent switches",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 36,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hbsg2",
              "name": "Description",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Built from A, with B and C as modes rather than separate apps. 1) Sidebar: expanded or collapsed to a rail ( [ ). Collapsed gives B's focus feel without forcing ⌘K navigation. 2) View layout: every list (My work, a project, a repo) can be shown as List or Board, using the same toolbar, filters and grouping. 3) Item presentation: panel, modal or full page. All three render the same Item view built from the same sections; only the container and the arrangement change. Below ~760 px wide the sections stack in one column, and above it they split into content plus a properties column. A link to an issue opens the full page. Maximize ( ⇧F ) turns a panel or modal into it, and the default is a user setting.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
