                          ],
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "CFYQv",
                              "name": "Commit message",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Fixes #468.\n\n## Why\nStripe retries a failed delivery for up to three days, but only if we answer with a non-2xx. The worker caught the billing service's 5xx, logged it and answered 200, so Stripe considered the event delivered and it was lost. During the 14 October deploy that dropped 212 events.\n\n## What changes\n- webhooks/stripe.ts answers 503 when the billing service returns 5xx, and retries on our side first: exponential backoff from 500 ms, at most 5 attempts.\n- Events that exhaust the retries go to webhook_dead_letter with the payload and the last error, so they can be replayed.\n- scripts/replay-dead-letter.ts replays them. Idempotency keys make a replay safe.\n- New setting STRIPE_RETRY_MAX, default 5.\n\n## How it was tested\n- Unit tests for the backoff and for the 4xx path, which is not retried.\n- Replayed the 14 October events against staging: 212 of 212 applied once.\n\n## Rollout\nNo migration beyond the new table. Watch webhook.retry.count for the first day.\n\nCo-authored-by: Sofia Bauer <sofiab@fitloop.dev>",
                              "lineHeight": 1.5,
                              "fontFamily": "$mono",
                              "fontSize": 11.5,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
